tasks.description:
**Verification only — no production or test edit** (if a check fails, report it; do not fix another wave's file from here). `task_type` is recorded as `doc` because this task writes no code and no test file: the graph validator's code-writing rule is what requires a non-empty `touches_files`, and the gate's only artefact is its recorded result. If a check fails, report it rather than editing another wave's file. Run, and record the actual numbers in the task result:
(a) the full offscreen suite: `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` (a clean full run, not incremental — the shared test DB and the stale `pytest` shebang are recorded gotchas);
(b) the residue check **through the guard itself** — `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_d45_removal.py -q` runs both nets (AST: identifiers + string constants, over `ui/ services/ data/ ibkr/ config/`; plus the raw-text `ui/` twin) and the end-state test; print the survivor allow-list beside the totals — every survivor must still be present and the expected post-P5 numbers are **0 AST offences / 0 twin hits**. Do **not** write a fresh 80-token sweep: the guard carries one deliberate, file-scoped exemption (`_ALLOWED_IN_FILE`: `stop_loss`/`take_profit` -> `{data/db.py}`, consulted via `_allowed_in(rel, token)`), because the drop migration must name the columns it removes (`data/db.py:200`, `for _column in ("stop_loss", "take_profit")` inside `_migrate_schema`). A hand-rolled sweep that ignores `_allowed_in` reports exactly those two — that is **not** residue and not a failure: it is the one legitimate occurrence, no code uses either column and no DDL creates either column. Any per-file breakdown is produced by calling the guard's own helpers, never by copying its token list;
(c) `AC-D46.3` reproduced **per code**: a real offscreen `MainWindow` (mocked `IBApiClient.connect`, temp `DB_PATH`) driven through `_on_error` with `reqId` matching no live session for each of 201, 103 and 202, asserting the status bar carries `[code]` **and** TWS's own text, then asserting `classify_error`'s four code sets and the `8000` ms duration are unchanged;
(d) the import/launch probe: `python -c "import ui.main_window, data.models"`, an app start under `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`, and `python -c "import ibkr.orders"` raising `ModuleNotFoundError`;
(e) the migration reproduced on a **pre-P5 fixture** with `DB_PATH` exported to a temp file (memory 2026-10-15/ESC-043): row counts before/after, `sqlite_master` (the unique index), `PRAGMA foreign_key_list`, `foreign_key_check`, `integrity_check`, and a second open that is a no-op;
(f) no `placeOrder`/`cancelOrder`/`reqGlobalCancel` call site and no new order/cancel/protection surface in `ui/ services/ data/ ibkr/ config/`;
(g) the doc-trail grep: no `kept`, `no migration` or `retained` claim within three lines of a `stop_loss`/`take_profit` token across the six files (`USAGE.txt`, `usage.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/plan.md`, `docs/codebase-map.md`, `docs/requirements/requirements.md` — the last two are Plan/Requirements-owned and must already carry their markers; a hit there is reported, not edited);
(h) record the migrated guard's **pre-P5** failure set beside the post-P5 numbers as the discrimination evidence: **41 AST offences across 10 files** (`ui/main_window.py` 14, `ibkr/orders.py` 7, `services/sound_service.py` 5, `data/models.py` 3, `ibkr/bridge.py` 3, `ibkr/client.py` 3, `ibkr/account.py` 2, `ibkr/pacing.py` 2, `data/db.py` 1, `config/settings.py` 1) and **40 twin hits on 27 lines, all `ui/main_window.py`** — measured before wave 1 and independently re-run by the Validator; never claim a run that did not happen.
